#
# INDEX.json records `cassette_sha256` over the LITERAL BYTES of each recorded body, so a
# digest here is a claim about the committed artefact and not about its parsed content.
# Git's default `text=auto` detection classifies these files as text and normalises their
# newlines on the way in, which is how the store came to be recorded on a Windows
# workstation as CRLF, committed as LF, and read back in CI as bytes that could not hash to
# the digest beside them. `-text` withdraws that permission in both directions: the bytes
# committed are the bytes checked out, on every platform.
#
# `diff` is deliberately left ON. These are evidence files and an edit to one must remain
# legible in review; suppressing the diff would hide exactly the change this store exists
# to make visible.
#
# The producer holds the same rule from the other side:
# make_live_cassettes.canonicalise_store_bytes writes UTF-8 with LF regardless of host, and
# test_live_cassettes.test_the_store_is_committed_in_one_byte_encoding fails if a carriage
# return ever reappears.
* -text
